{"repositoryId":1306263218,"availability":"available","full":"electrohyun/smocket","name":"smocket","description":"🐈 Mock Socket.IO without a server.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":5,"created":"2026-07-20T05:50:48Z","updated":"2026-10-12T11:10:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://smocket-site.vercel.app","topics":["frontend","mock","mocking","socket-io","test-utilities","testing","typescript"],"demo":"https://smocket-site.vercel.app/demo","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:45:43.210Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T11:45:43.210Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T11:45:43.210Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T11:45:43.210Z","stars":4,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["When developing a Socket.IO frontend, you need to see several clients connect, join rooms, and receive different events. Before the backend event API is ready, there is nowhere in the frontend to run that flow, so work on the multi-client UI has to wait too.","A hand-written socket object can call a listener, but it usually has one handler map. It cannot choose recipients from room membership, namespace, a broadcast target, or the lifetime of an acknowledgement. An HTTP mock can define requests and responses, but it does not own that long-lived connection state or Socket.IO routing.","A separate local Socket.IO server is accurate, but it also needs another process, configuration, and a reachable host. That makes it awkward for isolated component development and static previews, especially when the frontend only needs the application event layer."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electrohyun/smocket/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8fcfef7c6b1a0eedd7cda0dff88d5842eecfcd9d33e6c87a91dc21adb53ae7bd","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T11:45:43.344Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:45:43.344Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"When developing a Sock